### Sample requests (VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP client).
### Start the stack with ./run.sh first; it seeds demo data.
@proxy = http://localhost:8000
@target = http://localhost:8001

### 1. Discover the target API endpoints from its swagger docs (MUC1.4)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/resources/sync

### 2. List resources
GET {{proxy}}/admin/resources

### 3. Create a consumer group with its first consumer (MUC1.1)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups
Content-Type: application/json

{"group_name": "premium", "consumer_ids": ["alice"]}

### 4. Add a consumer to a group (MUC1.2)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/consumers
Content-Type: application/json

{"id": "bob", "consumer_group_id": 1}

### 5. Create a rate limiting policy (MUC1.3 / MUC4)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/policies
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "five-per-minute", "rate_limiting_strategy": "fixed-window", "number_of_requests": 5, "time_period": "minute"}

### 6. Supported strategies
GET {{proxy}}/admin/policies/strategies

### 7. Update a policy (MUC4) — invalidates the policy cache (MUC5)
PATCH {{proxy}}/admin/policies/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"number_of_requests": 20}

### 8. Create a resource group
POST {{proxy}}/admin/resource-groups
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "checkout", "description": "cart endpoints", "resource_ids": [11, 12]}

### 9. Assign a policy to one resource (MUC1.5)
POST {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups-policies
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_group_id": 1, "relationship_type": "resource", "policy_id": 2, "resource_id": 3}

### 10. Assign a policy to a resource group
POST {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups-policies
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_group_id": 1, "relationship_type": "resource_group", "policy_id": 2, "resource_group_id": 1}

### 11. Assign one policy to all resources of a consumer group
POST {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups-policies
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_group_id": 1, "relationship_type": "all_resources", "policy_id": 2}

### 12. List / update / delete assignments of a consumer group (MUC2)
GET {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups-policies?consumer_group_id=1

###
PATCH {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups-policies/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"policy_id": 3}

###
DELETE {{proxy}}/admin/consumer-groups-policies/1

### 13. Mint a bearer token for a consumer (development helper)
# @name token
POST {{proxy}}/admin/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{"consumer_id": "free-user-1"}

### 14. Call the target API through the proxy (CUC1). Repeat >10 times for a 429.
GET {{proxy}}/orders/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}

### 15. Write through the proxy
POST {{proxy}}/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "pen"}

### 16. Target API directly (bypasses the limiter; for comparison)
GET {{target}}/orders/1
